  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1219 AM CDT Sun Aug 16 2026\n\nThe hot and dry doldrums of summer will continue for the next \nseveral days as a 596dam upper-level ridge will remain the \ndominant feature across the southern US. As the upper-level flow \nbecomes more zonal across the northern tier of the US, the ridge \nwill retrograde westward by Tuesday and become centered over west \nTexas through Wednesday. The warmest days look to be Tuesday and \nWednesday when 850mb temperatures will increase to 25-27 deg C and\nthe ridge is directly overhead. There is a medium to high \n(40-80%) chance for high temperatures to exceed 105 degrees across\nthe Big Country and Concho Valley, so heat advisories could be \nneeded. High temperatures will be around 100 elsewhere.\n\nFor Thursday and Friday, the ridge will shift further westward \nand become centered over the Four Corners region. While \ntemperatures may be a few degrees lower, this likely will not \nbring much overall relief from the heat for most areas. In \naddition, a weak trough axis will move into the Southern Plains in\nplace of the ridge. This will push a cold front southward into \nNorth Texas on Friday, which could introduce some low (<20%) rain \nchances into Saturday for the Big Country.",
